<title>ITALY: CYCLING-TIRRENO-ADRIATICO FOURTH STAGE RESULTS.</title>
<headline>CYCLING-TIRRENO-ADRIATICO FOURTH STAGE RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>TERNI, Italy 1997-03-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading results in the</p>
<p>fourth 117-km stage of the Tirreno-Adriatico cycle race on</p>
<p>Sunday (Italian unless stated):</p>
<p>1. Giovanni Lombardi two hours 35 minutes 48 seconds</p>
<p>2. Jan Svorada (Czech Republic)</p>
<p>3. Glenn Magnusson (Sweden)</p>
<p>4. Robbie McEwen (Australia)</p>
<p>5. Marcel Wust (Germany)</p>
<p>6. Mario Traversoni</p>
<p>7. Martin Hvastija (Slovenia)</p>
<p>8. Elio Aggiano</p>
<p>9. Fabrizio Guidi</p>
<p>10.Sergei Outschakov (Ukraine) all same time</p>
<p>Overall standings:</p>
<p>1. Roberto Petito 15 hours 50 minutes 19 seconds</p>
<p>2. Gianluca Pianegonda same time (0.14 seconds behind)</p>
<p>3. Beat Zberg (Switzerland) 12 seconds</p>
<p>4. Massimiliano Gentili 23 seconds</p>
<p>5. Davide Casarotto 24 seconds</p>
<p>6. Francesco Frattini 26 seconds</p>
<p>7. Vassily Davidenko (Russia) 35 seconds</p>
<p>8. Luc Leblanc (France) 41 seconds</p>
<p>9. Massimo Donati 55 seconds</p>
<p>10.Michele Bartoli two minutes 47 seconds</p>
</text>
